/-! # Definitional Closure Manifest of the Pinned Statements, Pinned

The audit modules imported here freeze the printed statements of their theorems
(`#guard_msgs` on `#check`), which name definitions, predicates and hypothesis
records by name only: a change to the body of a definition or to the fields of
a structure a statement names leaves every such pin passing. This manifest pins
their meaning. Its roots are exactly the constants those audits' `#check`
commands name (`Ix.Cert.{MultiStark,MultiStarkRefinement,Aggr,Compression,
Compression.Bls12381}.Audit`, `Ix.Cert.Compression.StarkShrinkerAudit`
and `Aiur.Audit`); every definition, inductive, constructor, recursor and
statement type reachable from them is canonically serialized and hashed with
SHA-256 (`IxCK.Kernel.Audit.ClosureManifest`); theorem proofs are not entered.
Any change to the definitional closure changes the digest and fails the build
of this module. (`Ix.Cert.AiurCompression.Audit`'s statements have their own
manifest, `Ix.Cert.AiurCompressionClosureManifest`.)

Updating it (only with a reviewed change to the statements or the definitions
they name): build this module with
`IX_STATEMENT_CLOSURE_MANIFEST_WRITE=Tests/Fixtures/statement-closure-manifest.txt`,
then update `pinnedDigest` below with the reported SHA-256 digest and commit both.
-/

